, \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b707f729-f629-4867-9965-f2ea0e303433","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED as change 1085, merged to main.\n\nBoth passages now name the two jobs that actually exist (clean-core-wheel, optional-extras), and docs/llm-framework.md records where the AST import-linter half went — its two test files run in the default suite on every matrix cell, guarded by the collection test in tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py — so a reader who remembers the deleted job does not conclude the check was dropped.\n\nOn the AC 'no reference to a per-extra, union, or import-linter JOB remains': two greps still hit, and both are intentional descriptive text rather than job references.\n  - docs/llm-framework.md: 'The AST import-linter half is no longer a dedicated job: ...' — this IS the sentence a sibling AC requires.\n  - .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:134: 'clean-core-wheel + optional-extras (per-extra venvs + union)' — verified verbatim against the job's own name: field, which is 'optional extras isolate (per-extra venvs + union)'. It describes what the single job does.\nChecked by reading the job definitions rather than trusting the grep.\n\nVerification: make lint (actionlint over all workflows) PASS; pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py 9 passed.\n\nOut of scope and deliberately untouched, both recorded in the plan and the commit:\n  - 'The optional surface is three extras' in the same docs section is stale (rebar._optional.EXTRAS holds five; grounding and metrics are missing from both the count and the bullets). Fixing it needs new descriptive content for two extras — a content change, not a mechanical job-list correction. Left for a separate ticket and noted in session log 5eb0-52a3-45f0-43e5.\n  - docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/*.jsonl match the grep but hold captured historical AC text from plan-review experiments; editing them would falsify the experiment record.","timestamp":1785460566191519001}],"created_at":1785459315906408001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d3fa2fa8-a763-4073-9956-028cac458bd0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ad63-17ad-d545-45d4"},{"link_uuid":"f3a92de8-defa-4e9d-ad50-67a6ad4330ae","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a237-e911-ee71-463f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nTwo comments describe optionality CI jobs that no longer exist, left behind by tickets 2132 (change 1065) and ad63 (change 1066):\n\n- `docs/llm-framework.md:48-49` says the lean-runtime contract is enforced by \"an AST import-linter + a clean-core-wheel job that asserts the heavy stack is *not* importable + per-extra and union jobs\". The `import-linter` JOB was deleted in 1065 (its 9 tests already run in all four `test` matrix cells, and a collection guard in `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` now pins that), and the `per-extra` matrix + `union` job were replaced in 1066 by a single `optional-extras` job running one venv per extra plus a joint union venv.\n- `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:134` describes the reusable it invokes as \"the lean-runtime / clean-core-wheel / per-extra / union contract\".\n\nThe reusable's actual jobs are now exactly `clean-core-wheel` and `optional-extras`.\n\nThese are comments and prose only -- no behavior depends on them -- which is precisely why they will rot silently. Both were flagged during the 1066 review and deliberately left out of that change's scope to keep its diff reviewable.\n\n## Approach\nCorrect both passages to describe the jobs that exist, and say where the import-linter half went so a reader who remembers it is not left thinking the check was dropped. Nothing else in either file changes.\n\nRejected alternative: fold these into 1066. That change was already replacing a matrix with hand-written bash across three files; adding doc edits to it would have made the diff harder to review for the silent-failure modes that mattered there.\n\nRejected alternative: also correct the adjacent \"The optional surface is three extras\" claim in the same `docs/llm-framework.md` section. It IS stale -- `rebar._optional.EXTRAS` holds five (`agents`, `eval`, `grounding`, `metrics`, `tracing`) and the section bullets only three. But fixing it properly means writing new descriptive content for `grounding` and `metrics`, which is a different kind of edit from correcting a job list. Left for a separate ticket so this one stays a mechanical correction.\n\n## Scope\n- `docs/llm-framework.md` -- the CI-enforcement clause in the \"Extras taxonomy\" section.\n- `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` -- the `optionality` job's leading comment.\n\nExplicitly NOT in scope: the \"three extras\" count above; `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/*.jsonl`, which contain captured historical AC text from plan-review experiments -- editing those would falsify the experiment record.\n\n## Testing\nNo testable behavior: both edits are comments/prose. `make lint` runs actionlint over all workflows, which parses the edited YAML; `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` covers the workflow wiring the comment describes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` no longer claims a per-extra or union job exists, and names the jobs that do (`clean-core-wheel`, `optional-extras`).\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` records that the AST import-linter check now runs in the default test suite rather than a dedicated job.\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`'s `optionality` job comment names the current jobs.\n- [ ] No reference to a `per-extra`, `union`, or `import-linter` JOB remains in `docs/` or `.github/`, excluding `docs/experiments/**` archival corpora.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` passes.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"correct the CI-enforcement clause naming removed jobs"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"correct the optionality job comment naming removed jobs"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","a237-e911-ee71-463f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0d8c55de-5727-44ed-a87f-b25f7fd9752b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"67b1-49ed-ba22-42b7","ticket_type":"task","title":"Fix prose describing the removed optionality CI jobs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["86c89ff7-c04e-4b78-9a7c-5ceac8bb9c4b","4781ec62-1f3c-4999-b4d8-a5ecf8e4805e","d3fa2fa8-a763-4073-9956-028cac458bd0","a6a65fe4-cedb-4c76-9a63-365d5e98fa01","427036fc-3b77-4c29-8ff0-c102f004f603","fc1689cb-0bff-43a0-a680-4f5aeb5b637f","f3a92de8-defa-4e9d-ad50-67a6ad4330ae","2508d8c0-a608-4157-983f-e7036229d8cf","b394de03-b836-4eab-afc0-785de9c4ca1b","0d8c55de-5727-44ed-a87f-b25f7fd9752b","e353347a-1f58-4360-9227-921b8d1a65f6"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659614718679001,"uuid":"121d6fe7-afcd-4734-8c46-73335bd0353a"}